Assignment 3 – Terminal Navigation Practice Sheet

Introduction

Terminal commands are used to create folders, files, copy files, rename files, and move between folders.

Commands

No.| Task| Command| PowerShell
1| Show current folder| "pwd"| "pwd"
2| List files| "ls"| "ls"
3| Show hidden files| "ls -la"| "ls -Force"
4| Create a folder| "mkdir practice"| "mkdir practice"
5| Enter the folder| "cd practice"| "cd practice"
6| Create an empty file| "touch index.html"| "ni index.html"
7| Create nested folders| "mkdir -p css/images"| "mkdir css/images"
8| Go up one level| "cd .."| "cd .."
9| Go to home directory| "cd ~"| "cd ~"
10| Copy a file| "cp index.html backup.html"| "cp index.html backup.html"
11| Rename a file| "mv backup.html old.html"| "mv backup.html old.html"
12| Delete a file| "rm old.html"| "rm old.html"
13| Delete a folder| "rm -r css"| "rm -r css"
14| Show file contents| "cat index.html"| "cat index.html"
15| Clear the screen| "clear"| "cls"
16| Open folder in VS Code| "code ."| "code ."

Practice Exercise

Step 1: Go to home directory
"cd ~"

Step 2: Create website folders
"mkdir -p website/css website/images"

Step 3: Create HTML and CSS files
"touch website/index.html website/css/style.css"

Step 4: Go into CSS folder
"cd website/css"

Step 5: Return to website folder
"cd .."

Step 6: List all files and folders
"ls -R"

Step 7: Rename index.html to home.html
"mv index.html home.html"

Step 8: Rename home.html back to index.html
"mv home.html index.html"

Step 9: Open the folder in VS Code
"code ."

Conclusion

I practised terminal commands to create folders, create files, move between folders, list files, rename files, and open a folder in VS Code. These commands are useful for web development.